+### Retiring the forms attached by older versions
+
+New forms are never stored, so the folder `data/files/blobs` stops growing. To remove the old ones safely (do it once, no hurry):
+
+1. `npm run upac:export` (the website can keep running). It copies every old form into `data/upac-export` (or the folder you give it, for example on another drive), names each file after its connection (`list.csv` shows the list) and checks every copy against its fingerprint. It can be run again; it only copies what is missing. Do not go on until it prints `Export complete`.
+2. Keep that folder safe; it is now the only copy of the old forms apart from your backups.
+3. `npm run upac:cleanup -- <that folder>` only checks and reports (nothing is changed).
+4. Stop the website, then `npm run upac:cleanup -- <that folder> --apply`. It first proves again that every form is in the folder, makes a copy of the database (`pace_it.sqlite.before-upac-cleanup-<time>`), and removes the old attachment records in one transaction. Start the website again.
+5. The old form files in `data/files/blobs` are removed by the nightly backup job once no kept backup refers to them, so the space comes back gradually as old backups age out (up to the weekly backup retention, 26 weeks by default). `data/files/upac` (plain copies from an even older version) can be deleted by hand once the export folder is checked.
